{"kind":"artifact","text":"The ui tree as main carries it at merge commit 8691ce3712d9cd7955ae98b031d7ba959069cc76, which landed the timestamp-resilience work approved by codex in b4b9530c and ratified in 2cd24da0.\n\nThe merge changed ui/src/components/ErrorBoundary.tsx, ui/src/components/EventTime.tsx, ui/src/lib/util.ts, ui/src/main.tsx and ui/test/dom.test.mjs. EventTime now checks a timestamp before formatting it and renders 'unreadable time' rather than throwing on a value outside the range a JavaScript Date can hold; an ErrorBoundary above the application catches any other render fault and offers a manual retry. The retry is manual on purpose, because the projection replays from the log and an automatic one would loop on a fault that has not cleared.\n\nSUCCESSION IS INCOMPLETE, DELIBERATELY. Step 5 asks me to retire every live artifact covering what this merge changed. The live artifact describing this path is 9dc0be22 at commit 9cbdf1ed, and I have not retired it, because five pages cite it: docs/concepts/components.md, docs/reference/architecture.md, docs/reference/gs/serve.md, docs/reference/limits.md and docs/reference/mcp/presence.md. Retiring it would leave all five pointing at a withdrawn record and take the docset gate red — the same failure that made main unbuildable for an hour and a half on 2026-08-12, with eleven pages. The guard added in ff6132ec refuses exactly this, and it is right to.\n\nSo this path knowingly carries two live artifacts until those pages are re-anchored onto this one and 9dc0be22 is retired. That is ordinary implementing work and it needs its own request; forcing it now with --cited-ok would be using the migration escape hatch for something that is not a migration. Until then a reader should treat this artifact as what main carries and 9dc0be22 as the predecessor still standing.\n\nThe candidate artifact 070e4f89 at this path names head 2f028fbe, which is now in main; it is superseded in substance by this record and should be retired in the same repair.\n\nThis rests on eab525cc at docs rather than on 9dc0be22, so that retiring the predecessor later does not make this record stale from birth.","body":{"commit":"8691ce3712d9cd7955ae98b031d7ba959069cc76","path":"ui"}}